    "text": "Consider two uniform discs of the same thickness and different radii&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>R</mi></math> made of the same material. If the ratio of their moments of inertia&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, respectively, about their axes is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is :",
